00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.069 align:start position:0%
 
today the former racing driver close  needs fitz will be testing audi's  revamped luxury sedan the a8  meets with praises the a8 saying it's  the ultimate in luxury audi says that a  wealth of technological innovations  enable this car to do everything better  than its predecessor  time for a short history lesson audi  introduced its v8 in 1988 but in terms  of roominess and comfort it couldn't  compete with bmw 7 series or mercedes s  series  six years later the first a8 came out  with the world's first aluminum chassis  in a serially produced luxury class  vehicle  the a8 got air suspension in 2002 the  increase in comfort helped audi to edge  out bmw 7 series and number of vehicles  registered in their class where it was  second only to mercedes s series  at the end of 2011 the newest generation  of a8s was launched with a facelift  there is even a 12 cylinder engine model  conceived for the russian and chinese  markets audi has focused a lot of  attention on developing the headlight  system  veronica starringer of audi explains the  a8s automatic bright lights function  the high beams aren't operated manually  she says  instead they are electronically  controlled  individual led elements turn on or off  sequentially to automatically protect  the eyes of oncoming drivers  the blinkers have changed too  a panel of leds light up the sequence to  point in the turning direction  we tested the new luxury sedan in the  sporty s8 version  with 4 liters of engine displacement the  8 cylinder gasoline engine produces 382  kilowatts and a whopping maximum torque  of 650 newton meters  the s8 rockets from 0 to 100 kilometers  an hour in just 4.1 seconds maximum  speed is 250 kilometers an hour  the manufacturer rates the car's fuel  consumption at 9.6 liters per 100  kilometers but that demands skillfully  restrained driving  cylinder on demand contributes to fuel  thrift if power needs are low the engine  uses only four of its eight cylinders  the s8 chassis is 10 centimeters lower  than in the normal a8  is impressed that the a8's big engine is  so quiet at any speed  the interior is luxurious materials and  workmanship are lavish with the controls  conveniently arranged  continues  the variety of materials adds to the  interior's deluxe feel  the broad central console stands out and  clearly separates the driver from the  front seat passenger  an eight-speed tiptronic automatically  controls the s8 transmission  the leather seats are electronically  adjusted to fit the needs and  preferences of driver and passengers  needs fit sums up the audi s8 is a very  sporty luxury sedan he has no complaints  about the engine's power the chassis or  the brakes he says he's tempted to take  the s8 under the racetrack for a lap  everything is so top-notch except the  price which could be a little lower  the s8 base price was 114 700 euros in  germany making it exactly 40 000 euros  more expensive than the basic a8 model  but it still cost 35 000 euros less than  the sporty amg mercedes s-class  kia plans to introduce its first fully  electric car to the market in the second  half of 2014.  the sole ev will fundamentally resemble  its gasoline-powered sibling but it will  have its own design  its range between charges will be 200  kilometers and an 81 kilowatt engine  with 285 newton meters of torque will  make it fun to drive  renewable energy is on a roll in the  auto industry one of the pioneers is  sean with its project seat also  the manufacturer has mounted 53 000  solar panels on the roof of its monterey  plant  that's the equivalent of forty football  fields and means avoiding seven thousand  tons of carbon dioxide emissions  mercedes recently brought out a new  mid-range coupe sedan  the cla 200 is large and sporty like its  big brother the cls a four-door coupe  our test driver matas kurat took a  closer look at the cla 200.  mata says mercedes always calls the cla  a mid-range coupe sedan but it actually  builds on daimler's compact series the  a-class matas is going to see how well  it fits the mid-range category  the car's big grill has mean looking  headlights and large air intakes  graceful lines flow together everywhere  underscoring the car's dynamism  nothing here seems out of place  the streamlined rear has a dual exhaust  and a well concealed rear view camera  but inside our tester finds one  incongruent detail  he likes the dashboard and all the  instruments the language of shape the  vents the materials used are all lovely  but the display in the middle of the  dash for the radio entertainment system  and navigation sticks out like a sore  thumb montes is sure this could have  been better integrated  the interior design is very reminiscent  of mercedes sls  the steering wheel speedometer and  decorative elements all have a sporty  feel  the design is clearly structured except  for the myriad buttons on the curvy  central console  it's a luxurious ride up front but what  about the back seats  mata says the back seat shows that the  car is based on the a-class and the  coupe like roof line means the back  seats aren't comfortable for tall  passengers  at least there's lots of room for  luggage mata says the cla's 470 liter  trunk really is mid-range level it's  only five liters smaller than the  c-class  for more sportiness in the cla you can  spend an extra two thousand euros for  the speed shift transmission our test  driver is pleased overall with the cla  the cla's handling really pleases mantis  who says the car hugs the road and you  don't even notice that it's a  front-wheel drive that's because the  power steering reduces the typical  front-wheel drive feel  our test car's 115 kilowatts of power  accelerated to a maximum of 230  kilometers an hour its eco start stop  automatic optimizes fuel consumption in  city traffic  mata's current summary  mercedes has really done a good job of  avoiding confusing the cla and the  c-class the clas and c have smaller  engines those with the same names are  simply a bit less powerful except for  the c200cdi and the cla200cdi  which have the same push the two series  are geared to different people the  c-class is the sensible car the more  versatile one but also a little more  expensive the difference in price is  between two thousand and five thousand  euros depending on the engine size the  cla in contrast is more for the  lifestyle oriented buyer who plans to  drive alone they are air aligned affairs  with a  our the foreign variant of our test car  with a seven-speed automatic  transmission costs 37 890 euros in  germany the basic model is available for  6 000 euros less  sorry  opel's black widow  in the late 1960s it spread fear and on  german race tracks  now it's back  it was a resurrected opal record and  racing gear black broad and brawny opal  and racing fans may remember the  legendary car from more than 40 years  ago here the replica heads out for its  first drive  the record see was the epitome of middle  class life white bread on wheels and  suddenly the ordinary family car was  leaving porsches in the dust and racing  greats like eric bitter and a young  nikki lauda were in the driver's seat  the recreated black widow takes to the  asphalt of the handling course at opel's  dudenhoffen test center  the modified engine has to be run in  before it'll show what it can do  opal's first post-war racing car was  built in russell's heim in 1967 without  gm's approval  it was a creation of opal designer  anatoly lapine  after a few successes on the track the  black widow mysteriously vanished  now opal classic's jens cooper has built  a replica of the original  he says the first step was getting  photos from anatoly lapine himself  hardly any other information was  available not from the archive nor  private sources but lapine provided a  flood of information  lapine personally drew up the rear axle  design on a meals on wheels menu  opal's classics department gave the  go-ahead and yens found a 1966 opel  record to serve as the basis  many of the black widows components had  been custom made and to make the replica  as true to the original as possible they  had to be made again the project took  three years  in 1967 a 180 horsepower engine and a  900 kilo car produced a sensational  power to weight ratio especially for a  dowdy opal sedan and for the time it  handled like a champion mag wheels and  the special rear axle design played  their part too  a counter flow head was put on the opal  four-cylinder engine to increase  performance  cooper explains that it had specially  cast manifolds and dual webber two  barrel carburetors and a special  camshaft to give it more oomph  with a special intake manifold it had  double the performance of a normal  record  it would be hard to tell the replica  from the original if the original black  widow could be found  team leader kirk bagman a former opel  dealer and racing legend in his own  right was looking after the car during  the time nikki lauda was driving it  he remembers the car was in the  courtyard without its engine  they had been on the formula 5 circuit  in europe and suddenly the car vanished  to this day nobody knows if it was  stolen or what exactly happened to it  the black widow's mysterious  disappearance makes its resurrection all  the more dramatic now its fans are  hoping the replica will be making the  rounds at classic car shows and giving  its contemporaries a run for their money  just like the original once did  you

